                "entry_id": "4a6f245a-f815-3cdd-8cc3-6ac54f442676",
                "word": "mort-terrain",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4183d5cb-8370-48fb-9d39-767fb40adad5",
                        "entry_id": "4a6f245a-f815-3cdd-8cc3-6ac54f442676",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "morts-terrains"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1c5cac82-4547-3346-ad79-d4420f391ed3",
                        "entry_id": "4a6f245a-f815-3cdd-8cc3-6ac54f442676",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Terrain qui ne contient aucune matière utile et qui augmente l’épaisseur de la couche à percer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Industrie minière"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d2b7970-3390-4e78-8a71-c2e532f9cb5d",
                                "sense_id": "1c5cac82-4547-3346-ad79-d4420f391ed3",
                                "text": "Les conditions de l’exploitation [de la houille] sont rendues plus onéreuses par ce fait, qu’en France les dépôts se trouvent enfouis sous des épaisseurs considérables de morts-terrains."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a66788d3-931e-491f-88b7-e2caffd93d43",
                                "sense_id": "1c5cac82-4547-3346-ad79-d4420f391ed3",
                                "text": "L'exploitation comporte trois phases successives (ou parfois simultanées) : la découverture, ou enlèvement des morts-terrains, l’extraction proprement dite, qui consiste en l'arrachement des blocs hors de la masse et, enfin, le halage et l’ébauchage de ces blocs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "30a31e35-01cf-4132-ac29-a1ec76855f16",
                                "sense_id": "1c5cac82-4547-3346-ad79-d4420f391ed3",
                                "text": "Dans les régions d’affleurement (flanc de côteau), où l’épaisseur des morts-terrains n’est pas très considérable, l’exploitation se fait avantageusement a ciel ouvert, après l'enlèvement de ces derniers."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "efbaae57-ecf5-4fee-9c93-b1cf911f4b24",
                        "source_entry_id": "4a6f245a-f815-3cdd-8cc3-6ac54f442676",
                        "source_sense_id": "1c5cac82-4547-3346-ad79-d4420f391ed3",
                        "target_lang_word": "overburden",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "overburden",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9a546079-23e4-3f7b-9213-1d7cd7c36201",
                                        "entry_id": "0babf7e6-048a-3103-bb0e-b2dd4cdfe3d8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To overload or overtax."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "814d5a2c-c455-4586-a4d0-f14fc1687eaa",
                                                "sense_id": "9a546079-23e4-3f7b-9213-1d7cd7c36201",
                                                "text": "In reality, the levels of work varied: some internationals seemed overburdened with tasks and responsibility, some seemed underburdened, and some faced apparently just the right amount of work."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ae174a6-a4eb-4e69-b468-4f223ba8adc0",
                                                "sense_id": "9a546079-23e4-3f7b-9213-1d7cd7c36201",
                                                "text": "He said the increase would avoid overburdening taxpayers who have subsidised the railways by £31 billion since the start of the Coronavirus pandemic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "overburden",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b0c44e4c-7dcf-3427-9a77-17a3e707fbe6",
                                        "entry_id": "490db27f-0421-304e-b16b-43676f5c7252",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The rock and subsoil that lies above a mineral deposit such as a coal seam, or any other underground feature."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebe6bde6-9757-4506-96cb-ec6cec3e3f10",
                                                "sense_id": "b0c44e4c-7dcf-3427-9a77-17a3e707fbe6",
                                                "text": "Before much progress was made with the inverts, however, the movement became accelerated, and it was decided to lighten the load over the tunnel by removing some of the soil, […]. This reduction in the overburden arrested the movement, and the inverting and centring were completed, and the tunnel opened again to traffic on April 9, 1949."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b28e0e6-6048-41a7-ab73-4d89d1f5f03e",
                                                "sense_id": "b0c44e4c-7dcf-3427-9a77-17a3e707fbe6",
                                                "text": "Such rocks have been changed by baking in a terrestrial pressure-cooker. Then they have been disinterred: kilometres of overburden must have been removed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2008f364-97c4-4fda-9727-97b8e2984243",
                                                "sense_id": "b0c44e4c-7dcf-3427-9a77-17a3e707fbe6",
                                                "text": "Settari (2002) and Osorio et al. (1999) also suggest that the analysis domain should include overburdens, sideburdens and underburdens for better accommodation of the coupling effects of stress changes and flow."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9b446007-ded8-3b0f-a4fa-88bbab419245",
                                        "entry_id": "490db27f-0421-304e-b16b-43676f5c7252",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sterile stratum that lies above the stratum being investigated"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
